WEBVTT

00:15.098 --> 00:19.853
June 5th, 1972.

00:20.520 --> 00:23.898
On a hot humid night,
deep in the southern United States,

00:24.566 --> 00:28.903
one baby let out his first cry
in a hospital.

00:30.321 --> 00:33.992
However, this baby took his last breath
in his mother's arms

00:34.075 --> 00:37.746
before even seeing the first light of day.

00:38.329 --> 00:41.875
Until this point in her life,
this young mother had a hard life,

00:41.958 --> 00:45.003
and felt hopelessly miserable.

00:45.086 --> 00:50.258
This baby had become
her only pride and joy,

00:50.341 --> 00:53.720
and her only hope for a bright future.

00:54.304 --> 00:58.141
Thus, she refused
to accept the baby's death.

00:59.392 --> 01:03.521
Before the doctor and the nurses
saw that the baby died,

01:03.605 --> 01:07.525
the mother slipped out of her bed
like a ghost.

01:08.234 --> 01:11.237
She found another baby
born on the same day,

01:11.321 --> 01:13.823
and left her dead baby in its place.

01:13.907 --> 01:15.617
She then kept the baby as her own.

01:16.785 --> 01:20.538
The swapped baby had a fraternal twin.

01:21.247 --> 01:24.542
She was never questioned,

01:24.626 --> 01:27.462
and no one suspected foul play.

01:31.674 --> 01:34.093
Mommy, whose grave is this?

01:34.177 --> 01:35.929
That's my birthday.

01:37.138 --> 01:38.264
He died the same day?

01:38.973 --> 01:39.808
Enrico,

01:41.643 --> 01:45.230
you had a younger brother.

01:45.814 --> 01:47.649
He was your twin,

01:48.900 --> 01:51.861
but he died at the hospital
moments after you were born.

01:53.363 --> 01:54.697
Pray for him.

01:55.824 --> 01:56.908
After his passing,

01:57.992 --> 02:00.829
we named him Domenic.

02:03.248 --> 02:05.250
1987

02:06.084 --> 02:08.545
Oh Lord, answer my plea.

02:09.045 --> 02:12.298
My brother passed away
on the day we were born.

02:13.341 --> 02:17.554
Why did fate choose him and not me?

02:18.555 --> 02:21.891
Why… must there be
happiness and misfortune?

02:22.892 --> 02:24.811
What is true happiness?

02:25.812 --> 02:29.149
Father Pucchi was
15 years old at the time.

02:29.232 --> 02:33.236
His paternal grandmother
was an Italian immigrant.

02:33.319 --> 02:38.241
She came from a family with ties
to a prestigious clan in Venice

02:38.324 --> 02:41.536
which hailed a well-known clergyman
in the 18th century.

02:41.619 --> 02:44.956
When the young man showed interest
in pursuing priesthood,

02:45.039 --> 02:47.792
no one spoke out against this decision.

02:53.339 --> 02:56.467
What did you do? Who are you?

02:58.303 --> 03:00.263
What are you doing here?

03:01.306 --> 03:02.223
Hey!

03:02.307 --> 03:03.683
Is this your book?

03:05.018 --> 03:08.187
This is a famous autobiography of a cleric
who had an affair with a married woman.

03:08.271 --> 03:11.274
He later left the church
and became a painter.

03:11.357 --> 03:15.236
Do clergymen read such books?

03:15.820 --> 03:18.489
Who are you, and how did you get inside?

03:18.573 --> 03:22.952
This ossuary is closed to the public
except on Sundays.

03:25.288 --> 03:28.833
You see, I'm allergic to sunlight.

03:29.584 --> 03:32.795
The sun won't set until 6:19 p.m. tonight.

03:33.379 --> 03:35.089
I'm unable to leave until then,

03:35.173 --> 03:37.050
so that's why I was resting here.

03:40.178 --> 03:41.346
All right.

03:41.429 --> 03:44.224
Is there anything I can do for you?

03:44.807 --> 03:46.059
No.

03:46.142 --> 03:47.310
I see.

03:48.102 --> 03:49.187
I pity you.

03:50.855 --> 03:53.024
I won't tell Father about this,

03:53.524 --> 03:55.360
so you should leave at sunset.

03:58.863 --> 04:01.282
You're an interesting fellow.

04:03.368 --> 04:04.285
What's that?

04:04.369 --> 04:06.079
You won't force me to leave?

04:06.162 --> 04:11.000
I could be a thief who snuck in
to steal the artwork here,

04:11.084 --> 04:12.669
or even worse.

04:12.752 --> 04:15.546
Or maybe you're just
saying that I can stay,

04:15.630 --> 04:18.216
but you're going to report me.

04:18.299 --> 04:19.759
Is that your wish?

04:21.135 --> 04:25.098
No thief would lie and say
that they're allergic to sunlight.

04:25.682 --> 04:28.393
Not even the devil
would tell a lie like that.

04:28.977 --> 04:30.228
Hold on.

04:30.311 --> 04:32.146
Did you sprain your ankle?

04:32.230 --> 04:34.482
Was that my fault? Are you hurt?

04:34.565 --> 04:35.942
Oh, no.

04:36.025 --> 04:39.028
It's not your fault. I was born with this.

04:39.779 --> 04:42.615
My left toes are bent,

04:42.699 --> 04:45.451
but I can walk around just fine.

04:48.663 --> 04:51.291
Do you believe in the force of gravity?

04:51.791 --> 04:55.586
You tripped on me for a reason.

04:57.755 --> 04:59.299
What are you saying?

05:04.679 --> 05:08.099
Take this stone arrowhead.

05:08.182 --> 05:12.103
If you have no use for it, that's fine.

05:12.812 --> 05:16.274
But isn't it gravity
that draws people to each other?

05:16.858 --> 05:21.279
I don't know
what impression you have of me,

05:21.362 --> 05:24.532
but I travel to meet people.

05:25.700 --> 05:28.369
If you ever wish to see me again,

05:28.995 --> 05:32.332
wish upon this arrow and call me.

05:32.415 --> 05:35.043
No matter how far in the future
that may be.

05:35.543 --> 05:36.586
Do you understand?

05:36.669 --> 05:39.297
Just keep me in your back burner.

05:40.965 --> 05:42.508
At sunset,

05:43.134 --> 05:44.969
I will leave.

05:54.353 --> 05:55.938
What's this?

05:56.689 --> 05:59.400
My foot! The toes!

05:59.984 --> 06:01.736
They're straight!

06:02.236 --> 06:04.572
Wait! Who are you?

06:09.035 --> 06:10.953
1988

06:11.829 --> 06:13.206
Father.

06:14.749 --> 06:15.750
Please hear me out.

06:16.918 --> 06:19.670
I must confess my sins.

06:20.254 --> 06:21.589
Sorry,

06:21.672 --> 06:23.174
let me go get the priest…

06:23.257 --> 06:27.512
My body is stricken with an illness.

06:28.638 --> 06:30.848
I don't have much longer.

06:31.557 --> 06:35.645
But my confession
isn't about this illness.

06:36.771 --> 06:39.440
It concerns my family.

06:40.483 --> 06:44.070
It was 16 years ago, on June 5th.

06:44.153 --> 06:48.866
My baby died,
so I took another woman's baby,

06:49.534 --> 06:54.580
and swapped the two babies
while no one was looking.

06:54.664 --> 06:56.582
I took one of the twins.

06:58.709 --> 07:03.089
I cannot express how terrible I feel
for the baby's mother.

07:04.257 --> 07:08.177
But I poured my heart
into raising this baby.

07:09.053 --> 07:10.805
I had a happy life.

07:10.888 --> 07:14.892
He grew up to be a great boy.

07:16.185 --> 07:19.188
Shouldn't I tell him that
he has a twin brother

07:20.064 --> 07:24.360
before I leave this world?

07:24.444 --> 07:26.863
What if I tell him the truth,

07:26.946 --> 07:29.615
and my son leaves me before I die?

07:31.951 --> 07:33.161
So…

07:33.244 --> 07:35.913
Do you know the other family?

07:36.873 --> 07:40.460
They live in a large estate
in the neighboring town.

07:41.502 --> 07:43.921
The couple's name is Pucchi.

07:46.924 --> 07:48.134
Seriously?

07:48.217 --> 07:51.137
What's so good about a juice delivery boy?

07:51.220 --> 07:52.138
Gross.

07:52.221 --> 07:53.473
I bet he's a coward.

07:53.556 --> 07:57.226
- I love that.
- Forget him, his family's probably poor.

07:57.310 --> 07:59.187
He doesn't even go to high school.

07:59.270 --> 08:01.230
That's why he works.

08:02.690 --> 08:04.525
Perla, isn't that your bag?

08:04.609 --> 08:06.235
He snatched it!

08:06.319 --> 08:07.945
Thief!

08:08.029 --> 08:09.614
Someone stop him!

08:17.038 --> 08:19.332
- Woo-hoo!
- Yes!

08:20.333 --> 08:21.918
Oh, crap!

08:22.001 --> 08:24.795
I broke the store window.

08:24.879 --> 08:27.423
I'll get fired from
this part-time delivery job.

08:27.507 --> 08:30.092
My school doesn't even allow
students to work.

08:31.177 --> 08:34.514
Weather Forecast's real name
is Wes Aquamarine.

08:35.139 --> 08:37.016
He was 16 at the time.

08:37.099 --> 08:39.227
He was innocent
in every sense of the word,

08:39.310 --> 08:41.729
and he relentlessly pursued justice.

08:42.355 --> 08:44.690
Well… Thanks.

08:45.274 --> 08:46.901
That was my bag he tried to steal.

08:48.027 --> 08:51.197
I'll tell everyone that
the thief smashed the window.

08:51.781 --> 08:53.908
- Really?
- Of course.

08:54.492 --> 08:55.493
Now go.

08:59.121 --> 09:01.290
I'm Wes.

09:01.374 --> 09:02.959
People call me Weather.

09:04.502 --> 09:05.586
Can I see you again?

09:10.591 --> 09:14.136
Two months have passed
since that confession.

09:14.220 --> 09:16.931
Father Pucchi was under distress.

09:18.057 --> 09:20.768
Though not yet appointed a priest,

09:20.851 --> 09:24.480
he is obliged to keep the privacy
of the believers.

09:25.481 --> 09:27.942
He must keep the confession a secret.

09:28.943 --> 09:29.944
Otherwise,

09:30.027 --> 09:33.322
he would be deemed unworthy
as a clergyman.

09:34.031 --> 09:38.869
That mother wants to
take her secret to her grave.

09:39.453 --> 09:42.623
Had I been able to
convince her to tell the truth,

09:43.207 --> 09:47.086
how will we cope,
and how will my younger brother react?

09:47.587 --> 09:50.089
Will we be able to
treat our families the same?

09:52.592 --> 09:53.509
I'm home.

09:54.010 --> 09:55.678
Welcome back.

09:55.761 --> 09:58.556
Why are you spaced out on the porch?

09:59.265 --> 10:00.808
Did something happen at school?

10:01.976 --> 10:04.061
Please, Enrico.

10:05.021 --> 10:07.440
Don't tell Mom and Dad about this!

10:07.523 --> 10:08.357
What?

10:08.441 --> 10:10.443
My grades are slipping.

10:10.526 --> 10:13.112
I'll make up for it,
but there's something on my mind.

10:15.448 --> 10:18.492
I'm dating someone.

10:19.910 --> 10:21.704
We met only two weeks ago,

10:21.787 --> 10:23.205
but I really like him.

10:24.040 --> 10:27.460
It's like our hearts are connected.
I've never felt like this.

10:29.420 --> 10:31.172
I'm happy for you, Perla.

10:33.007 --> 10:34.091
Enrico…

10:35.468 --> 10:37.053
Let me tell you how this went.

10:37.136 --> 10:40.556
Father Pucchi never told his sister Perla,

10:40.640 --> 10:44.894
that Weather was their biological brother.

10:46.354 --> 10:50.775
I want you to judge
the rest of the events.

10:51.400 --> 10:54.445
Who committed a sin?

10:55.029 --> 10:57.823
Is it the mother, who swapped the babies?

10:57.907 --> 10:59.200
Or is it Father Pucchi's parents?

10:59.283 --> 11:00.868
Is it Father Pucchi?

11:01.494 --> 11:04.121
Is it the younger brother Weather,
who knows nothing?

11:04.914 --> 11:08.959
Father Pucchi looked into Weather,
the man his sister loved.

11:09.627 --> 11:13.047
After learning the shocking truth,

11:13.130 --> 11:14.965
Father Pucchi had only one choice to make.

11:15.800 --> 11:20.221
I can't let my sister get hurt,
no matter what!

11:23.140 --> 11:27.478
You're that wealthy kid
who goes to divinity school.

11:27.978 --> 11:30.147
Should you be doing this?

11:30.231 --> 11:32.650
If you succeed, I'll give you double.

11:32.733 --> 11:34.860
I have two requests.

11:35.528 --> 11:37.446
One, do not ask any questions.

11:38.030 --> 11:40.449
Two, make them break up.

11:41.450 --> 11:43.869
If I can get some thugs to threaten Wes,

11:43.953 --> 11:45.955
he'll break up with my sister.

11:46.038 --> 11:48.958
That's all Perla will experience,

11:49.041 --> 11:51.627
nothing but an ordinary heartbreak.

11:51.710 --> 11:54.547
This won't leave a permanent scar.

11:55.589 --> 11:57.716
However, Father Pucchi
barely knew anything

11:57.800 --> 12:02.179
about this private investigator,
a jack of all trades.

12:02.763 --> 12:06.642
How keen he was to information,
nor the darkness he carried.

12:06.725 --> 12:12.857
It is the darkness this society had,
which was allowed by law a century ago.

12:13.441 --> 12:15.109
It is a despicable old history.

12:18.404 --> 12:22.283
I can't believe what I learned
about Wes's birth.

12:22.867 --> 12:27.288
In 1972, his mother married

12:27.371 --> 12:29.665
a black man in the city.

12:29.748 --> 12:33.377
That makes him the son of a black man.

12:35.504 --> 12:39.175
The private detective
gathered other zealots.

12:40.676 --> 12:42.219
Weather!

12:42.303 --> 12:44.346
Perla…

12:49.894 --> 12:51.812
What are you doing? You're all drunk!

12:51.896 --> 12:53.522
We won't hurt you.

12:53.606 --> 12:55.566
He's the one we need to punish.

12:55.649 --> 12:59.195
Come give me a kiss.

12:59.278 --> 13:02.406
One for this officer too!

13:02.490 --> 13:05.117
You're a whore pretending to be
a proper little missy.

13:05.201 --> 13:08.662
Fool around with whomever you want,

13:08.746 --> 13:13.792
but this bastard isn't allowed
to kiss you, not even a little.

13:18.380 --> 13:20.591
Your brother wanted this done.

13:21.842 --> 13:25.930
And as for the woman
who gave birth to you,

13:26.013 --> 13:30.017
we set her house on fire.

13:42.446 --> 13:46.700
Who was the one truly being punished?

13:47.701 --> 13:50.663
Was it Weather, Perla, or…

13:51.247 --> 13:54.375
They all tried to love in their own ways.

13:55.584 --> 13:57.169
These are the facts.

13:57.753 --> 14:00.965
Father Pucchi's love
brought the worst outcome.

14:02.049 --> 14:06.053
Weather was hung high
on a tree by a cliff,

14:06.136 --> 14:08.055
and left to die.

14:08.847 --> 14:11.433
Perla truly had a pure heart,

14:11.517 --> 14:15.938
which was filled with a soft breeze
until this moment.

14:16.021 --> 14:18.357
Their love was like the warm spring sun.

14:19.108 --> 14:20.025
However…

14:24.864 --> 14:27.825
In my heart,

14:29.201 --> 14:31.954
there will never be another drop of rain.

14:32.872 --> 14:34.915
And with those words,

14:35.499 --> 14:38.752
Perla threw herself down
into the lake below the cliff.

14:39.545 --> 14:43.883
She did not know
that Weather had a slight pulse.

14:53.976 --> 14:56.186
Why?

14:56.854 --> 14:58.689
How could this happen?

15:00.232 --> 15:03.611
Why did I pursue the path of priesthood?

15:03.694 --> 15:06.363
Why do people meet?

15:06.447 --> 15:08.032
Had they never met,

15:08.115 --> 15:10.534
this would have never happened.

15:11.535 --> 15:12.536
No!

15:16.790 --> 15:18.834
Stop that!

15:18.918 --> 15:22.296
Don't make the sign of the cross
at my sister!

15:25.925 --> 15:26.967
Dammit.

15:27.551 --> 15:31.138
Please, just don't take Perla's life!

15:31.221 --> 15:32.890
Perla is innocent.

15:32.973 --> 15:35.100
She only fell in love!

15:35.184 --> 15:38.812
I'll do anything to bring her back!

15:39.855 --> 15:43.692
I'm the one who should be punished!

15:43.776 --> 15:46.195
Do you believe in the force of gravity?

15:46.278 --> 15:49.239
We met for a reason.

15:50.950 --> 15:52.534
If you wish,

15:53.160 --> 15:55.329
come see me.

15:56.080 --> 15:57.039
It's him.

15:57.665 --> 15:59.667
That was his voice.

15:59.750 --> 16:01.251
I want to see him.

16:01.335 --> 16:05.881
He once healed my bent toes
in the ossuary.

16:07.132 --> 16:09.385
Why did I forget about him until now?

16:10.260 --> 16:12.262
That's right, he gave me…

16:12.846 --> 16:15.224
an arrowhead-like thing.

16:22.064 --> 16:24.984
What is going on?

16:26.527 --> 16:28.946
The arrowhead in my pocket?

16:29.029 --> 16:31.281
Once a life is lost,

16:31.365 --> 16:33.909
you cannot bring it back.

16:33.993 --> 16:36.161
But it's up to you.

16:36.662 --> 16:38.497
If you wish from deep within your heart,

16:38.580 --> 16:41.792
you can retrieve her memory.

16:41.875 --> 16:44.294
It's the memories of her heart.

16:44.878 --> 16:47.339
This is your awakening.

16:59.184 --> 17:01.103
Who the hell are you?

17:01.186 --> 17:04.606
The idiot who wanted
an affair investigated?

17:04.690 --> 17:08.110
If you don't want to get shot,
show your dirty face--

17:09.820 --> 17:11.238
What's this?

17:11.321 --> 17:13.949
If you know, then tell me.

17:14.033 --> 17:15.075
What?

17:15.159 --> 17:16.952
I heard you know everything.

17:17.536 --> 17:20.456
What made these snails emerge
out of the blue?

17:21.040 --> 17:23.250
Where do they come from?

17:23.876 --> 17:25.878
Why is it only happening near me?

17:26.503 --> 17:28.255
Who the hell are you?

17:28.922 --> 17:31.425
You said Perla's brother
asked you to split us.

17:31.508 --> 17:32.676
Is that true?

17:32.760 --> 17:35.012
No, you can't be…

17:38.682 --> 17:42.436
What are these snails?

17:47.733 --> 17:49.860
Damn. I knew it, I can't die.

17:52.738 --> 17:54.656
The gunpowder is soaked.

17:55.282 --> 17:56.700
But only when I try to shoot myself.

17:57.701 --> 17:59.828
Why am I still alive?

18:00.788 --> 18:03.373
Weather was full of rage.

18:03.957 --> 18:07.086
He was enraged at those
who persecuted him,

18:07.836 --> 18:10.047
at the fact that he was alive,

18:10.631 --> 18:14.301
and that he couldn't save Perla.

18:16.053 --> 18:18.722
Once Weather learned about Perla's death,

18:18.806 --> 18:20.641
he jumped off the cliff.

18:21.225 --> 18:23.602
Just then,
there was a strong gust of wind.

18:25.896 --> 18:28.774
He also tried to drown himself
in the lake,

18:29.358 --> 18:31.985
but the waves brought him back to shore.

18:33.320 --> 18:36.990
Why won't you let me die with Perla?

18:43.914 --> 18:47.459
His anger was one of despair.

18:47.543 --> 18:52.714
His vengeance spread to all,
not just to the townspeople.

18:55.008 --> 18:56.468
On the fourth night,

18:56.552 --> 18:59.596
a horde of snails swarmed the town.

19:00.180 --> 19:02.015
Why snails?

19:02.099 --> 19:04.101
Where did they come from?

19:04.184 --> 19:06.812
No one knew.

19:07.855 --> 19:09.982
The only one who understood
the cause of this incident

19:10.566 --> 19:14.153
was Father Pucchi,
who woke up in a hospital.

19:15.154 --> 19:17.406
Wes… no, Weather did this.

19:17.489 --> 19:19.366
My brother isn't dead.

19:19.449 --> 19:21.326
We are twins.

19:21.410 --> 19:24.496
My awakening led to his.

19:25.080 --> 19:30.335
Just as I sought her memory,
so did Weather, though subconsciously.

19:30.919 --> 19:34.715
If these snails are here to
crawl up my arm,

19:34.798 --> 19:37.342
then I have to go kill my brother.

19:38.635 --> 19:41.096
I will resort to any and every method
from now on.

19:41.180 --> 19:43.265
I will even take lives.

19:44.266 --> 19:46.935
Once my score with Weather is settled,

19:47.019 --> 19:48.812
I will go see him.

19:49.438 --> 19:51.273
His name is Dio.

19:51.815 --> 19:54.067
Why do people's paths cross?

19:54.151 --> 19:56.653
If anyone can tell me, it's him.

19:57.696 --> 19:58.864
I must know it.

19:58.947 --> 20:03.035
The answer to this question
is the strongest power in this world.

20:03.619 --> 20:05.245
It must also be the truth.

20:09.416 --> 20:10.500
Are you satisfied?

20:11.043 --> 20:14.838
Your sister Perla died
because of your request.

20:15.339 --> 20:16.173
And…

20:16.757 --> 20:18.675
I can't suppress my rage.

20:18.759 --> 20:20.844
We have a score to settle.

20:21.428 --> 20:22.512
You're wrong.

20:22.596 --> 20:25.390
It's because I am your older brother.

20:26.558 --> 20:29.019
But that ends today.

20:29.102 --> 20:32.314
Weather, meet your end.

20:38.695 --> 20:41.740
Weather, you are in my way.

20:42.324 --> 20:43.450
Now die,

20:43.533 --> 20:45.744
and take those rainbows with you.

20:45.827 --> 20:49.790
Vanish with Perla and all your memories.

20:50.374 --> 20:53.961
A man with no memories
might as well be dead.

20:54.044 --> 20:58.131
Live as if you're dead trapped in a cage.

21:04.471 --> 21:07.641
Inmate MA152403.

21:08.141 --> 21:09.476
Imprisoned!

21:12.062 --> 21:14.564
My sole purpose in life

21:14.648 --> 21:16.984
is to settle my score with him.

21:18.026 --> 21:20.862
So you've been revived.

21:20.946 --> 21:22.656
Your memories returned!

21:22.739 --> 21:26.827
But I thought you were
going to meet up with Jolyne!

21:27.869 --> 21:31.498
I'm only with you to find Jolyne!

21:31.581 --> 21:33.834
You shouldn't go find Jolyne.

21:33.917 --> 21:35.502
It'll be a waste of time.

21:35.585 --> 21:36.545
Moreover,

21:36.628 --> 21:39.214
I need someone to finish me off.

21:40.882 --> 21:42.175
Kill me.

21:42.884 --> 21:45.137
I'm counting on you, Anastasia.

21:46.680 --> 21:48.640
That's why these beetles are called
snail eaters!

21:48.724 --> 21:51.268
These buggers!

21:56.773 --> 21:57.691
Get in, guys!

21:59.901 --> 22:01.903
They're coming in through the cracks!

22:01.987 --> 22:03.322
What do we do, Jolyne?

22:03.905 --> 22:06.491
Whether inside or outside the car,

22:06.575 --> 22:09.828
it's over once we get devoured.

22:10.412 --> 22:13.165
We'll go meet up with Weather
as we're being eaten!

23:41.294 --> 23:46.299
Subtitle translation by: Megumi Hunter
